# Python Backend Standards

- Keep route handlers thin and move business logic to `services/` or `models/`.
- Validate all external inputs at the boundary and return clear error messages.
- Use explicit HTTP status codes (`400`, `401`, `403`, `404`, `422`, `500`).
- Use structured logging; avoid ad-hoc `print` for operational paths.
- Keep functions focused and avoid hidden side effects.
- Preserve backward compatibility for response schemas unless migration is explicit.
